---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';
import { url } from '../lib';
---

<Layout
  title="Player Support | Encrypted Cat Games"
  description="Get help with The Cradle games, report a bug, or contact Encrypted Cat Games."
>
  <section class="container page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Player support</p>
    <h1>A light when you need it.</h1>
    <p>Help with The Cradle: Episode 01 and The Cradle: Trick-or-Treat.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container support-grid section">
    <div>
      <h2>Before you send a signal.</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details open>
          <summary>How do I play on iPhone or iPad?</summary>
          <p>
            The Cradle: Episode 01 is coming soon to the App Store as a paid app
            for iPhone and iPad (iOS 18 or later). Until then, and for
            Trick-or-Treat, play in Safari from the game’s itch.io page. For
            Episode 01 on iPhone, use Share → Add to Home Screen, then launch
            from the new icon to play without browser bars. On iPad, use the
            game’s full-screen button. Rotate your device to landscape.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href={url('games/')}>
            Find your game
          </a>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>The game runs slowly or won’t load.</summary>
          <p>
            Try a current browser, close other tabs, and reload the game. In
            Episode 01, lower graphics quality in Settings. If it still fails,
            send us your device model, operating system, browser version, and
            the point where loading stops.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where can I adjust controls and comfort settings?</summary>
          <p>
            Episode 01 includes graphics, brightness, sensitivity, key
            rebinding, and interface size settings. Its Comfort settings offer
            options for a more comfortable experience. Headphones are
            recommended; you can also use subtitles.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I report a bug?</summary>
          <p>
            Tell us which game you played, your device and operating system,
            browser or app version, what you expected, and what happened
            instead. Include steps to reproduce and any error text. Avoid
            including passwords or personal account information.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where are the iPhone and iPad App Store versions?</summary>
          <p>
            The Cradle: Episode 01 is coming soon to the App Store. The link
            will appear on the <a href={url('games/episode-01/')}>game page</a>{' '}
            as soon as it is live. Until then, the game pages link to itch.io.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I restore my purchase or reinstall the app?</summary>
          <p>
            Episode 01 on the App Store is a one-time purchase. To reinstall,
            sign in with the same Apple ID and download it again from the App
            Store at no charge. Saves live on your device: deleting the app
            deletes them, and they come back if you restore the device from an
            iCloud or computer backup made while the app was installed.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I play with a controller?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. Episode 01 plays with a game controller, such as an Xbox or
            PlayStation pad or a Steam Deck, menus included. On iPhone and iPad,
            pair the controller in iOS Settings → Bluetooth; the game’s
            Controller settings appear once it connects.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does the app use Game Center?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes, for achievements, and it is optional. If you are signed in to
            Game Center, your achievements and progress show there and
            achievements unlocked on another device signed in to the same
            account come back to the game. If you are not, you play as normal
            and the game still keeps its own achievements.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="support-form">
      <h2>Contact support.</h2>
      <p>Tell us what happened. We’ll reply to the email you provide.</p>
      <ContactForm />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
